[[1,1923566,0,1,4,-3,"2015-08-19T18:03:37","Imapopulistnow","[e]",[],"<p>Easy to say after the fact and after the risk of a massive Great Depression has been avoided. People must be forgetting how it was a few years back and they obviously are not able to comprehend how bad it would have gotten. QE sucks. But, no one had a better plan and those purists who say the markets should have been allowed to clear themselves are pollyannas who are not calculating in how low the economy would have had to go and how long it would have taken for the economy to dig out. More rapid growth? Sure, it would be easy to experience high rates of growth after an economy has been cut in half. But we would probably be worse off today as that rapid growth would still be catching up to what was lost is the economic collapse.</p>"],[1,1931640,0,0,0,0,"2015-08-19T23:38:00","refugee610","",[],"<blockquote>\n<p>zerohedge.com</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Not a credible source, please post this in <a href=\"/v/politics\">/v/politics</a> and find a better source (if there even is one) to put in <a href=\"/v/news\">/v/news</a>. I'm sure if this is actually news we can find a better source to post here.</p>"],[2,1941872,1931640,0,0,0,"2015-08-20T09:38:07","oswald_spengler","",[],"<p>They quoted directly from the St Louis paper <a href=\"http://www.scribd.com/doc/275145522/St-Louis-Fed-Qe-Study\">http://www.scribd.com/doc/275145522/St-Louis-Fed-Qe-Study</a></p>\n<p>Sure there's lot of doom and gloom but you'll find plenty of respected people in the financial world who've reference zerohedge at one point or another. I mean have you noticed the same-same of most of the financial press. Recovery is coming, it's here... or just around the corner. Trust us.</p>\n<p>The proof that things are fucked is right in front of you. Interest rates at fuck all for so long is more telling than anything IMO. </p>\n<p>I mean the fucking BIS comes out with statements that things are fucked. I've got the last of my $ out of the market a few months ago. I sleep easier as night having no counter party risk. </p>"],[1,1934430,0,0,0,0,"2015-08-20T01:48:10","RedditSucksNow","[e]",[],"<p><a href=\"http://www.cnbc.com/2015/08/18/st-louis-fed-official-no-evidence-qe-boosted-economy.html\">Another source</a> that actually explains WTF QE means.</p>"]]
