[[0,429540,0,2,0,2,"2015-08-19T17:00:29","somenonewho","",[],"","Any Chance to put another 3.5 in that cage?","https://veuwer.com/i/329w,329x,329y","buildapc"],[1,1924084,0,1,0,1,"2015-08-19T18:25:42","setitimer","[e]",[],"<p>Does the bottom of the cage have holes that would match the screw holes on the bottom of the drive? 3.5&quot; hard drives have screw holes for mounting on the underside as well as on the sides.</p>"],[2,1926113,1924084,0,0,0,"2015-08-19T19:51:05","somenonewho","[e]",[],"<p>Yeah I saw that and no it doesn't. Well seems like it's just made for 1 disk ... I wanted to convince my mom to buy one new bigger disk anyway.</p>"],[3,1926822,1926113,0,0,0,"2015-08-19T20:21:44","setitimer","[e]",[],"<p>The wider part there at the bottom of the drive cage looks like it is meant to take some sort of drive rails. On older PCs, you would attach rails to the drive, then slide the drive into the cage with the rails in the slots. The rails had a lever or clip system on them that kept them from sliding out of the cage. \n</p>\n<p>What make / model of computer is this? You can probably buy replacement rails on eBay if you don't have them.</p>"]]
